  "result": "Defaults set through `default_map` now reach subcommands, including subcommands of nested groups. The full test suite passes (1907 passed, 102 skipped). The new test fails without the fix and passes with it.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`src/click/core.py:392`** (the fix): a subcommand's context now uses `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`, the entry for its own name, instead of the parent's whole map. So `{\"sub\": {\"port\": 5000}}` now gives `sub --port` a default of 5000.\n- **`tests/test_context.py`**: added `test_default_map_subcommands`, covering a direct subcommand and a subcommand inside a nested group.\n- **`CHANGES.md`**: 8.5.0 is already marked as released, so I added a new \"Version 8.5.1 \u2013 Unreleased\" section for the entry. Rename it if you have a different version in mind.\n\nNothing is committed yet.",
